 Small operations repository for the log retention job.
 
-`bin/archive-logs.sh SERVICE` packs the logs of one service from `logs/` into a dated
-tarball under `archives/`. It runs from cron on the log host every night.
+## Usage
 
-Archives are pruned by hand today.
+```
+bin/archive-logs.sh [--keep-days N] SERVICE [SERVICE...]
+```
+
+Packs the logs of each named service from `logs/` into a dated tarball
+(`archives/SERVICE-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz`). Several services can be given in one run.
+Run it from the repository root; it runs from cron on the log host every night.
+
+- Service names are validated up front (letters, digits, `_`, `.`, `-`; must start
+  with a letter or digit). If any name is invalid, nothing is archived.
+- `--keep-days N` (`N` a non-negative integer) removes `*.tar.gz` files in
+  `archives/` whose modification time is more than `N` days old. Pruning happens
+  only after all new archives are written, so a failed run never prunes. Without
+  the option nothing is removed.
+- On success it prints one summary line, for example:
+  `archived 2 service(s): api web; pruned 1 archive(s) older than 30 day(s)`
+  (the `pruned` part appears only with `--keep-days`).
+- Exit status: `0` success, `64` bad usage or invalid input, `1` other failure
+  (for example a service with no log directory).
+
+Example:
+
+```
+bin/archive-logs.sh --keep-days 30 api web
+```
